id:                     E1694
trigger_tool: conan|static-library|runtime-data
phase: package|consumer-test
error_signature: "static package has no run trait but library API requires packaged data|palette XML not found in consumer environment"
severity:               2
category:               conan, linkage, runtime-data, static
match_keywords: static library, runtime data, package_type_traits, runenv_info, palette, consumer
title: A static library can still require a Conan runtime trait and packaged data path
root_cause: >
  Static linking removes a shared ELF loader dependency, not runtime file
  dependencies. Conan may otherwise treat a static-library package as purely
  build-time and omit its run environment, leaving installed APIs unable to
  locate packaged XML or other data even though compilation and linking pass.
affected_scope: Static libraries whose public APIs load package-owned data files at runtime
verification_cmd: "declare package_type_traits run=true, publish a package-relative runenv path, then execute an installed consumer that actually loads the data through the library API"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: preserve-runtime-data-contract-for-static-package
rec_description: >
  Package data under a stable relative directory; set the Conan run trait and
  runenv variable to the installed package path; exercise the real API under
  conanrun. Test a missing-data negative separately when diagnosing; do not
  claim success from a mere file-exists check.
  Runtime-data consumer success on a developer machine also does not prove
  that its source build is closed over declared inputs. A source-bundled
  canonicalizer may be masked by an ambient Automake helper; remove that
  hidden dependency and execute the hash-bound bundled helper before claiming
  the static archive/data consumer is reproducible on a minimal worker.
rec_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: "assume a static library has no runtime assets and test only linking"
forbid_1_reason: the executable can link while API calls fail when data is absent
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E14848-draft-2501_91199785.md
source_event: flam3/3.1.1 historical runtime-data run flam3-w3-20261003T174537Z; CI80120 showed an undeclared canonicalizer dependency; repaired run flam3-ci9-w3-20261010T101200Z passed clean Conan create and installed consumer, log sha256 61a9eb301586b90141fd3f30b38445ea219add229854f417148c9941a96d7a2a
last_updated: 2026-10-12
rec_impl:               manual
authors:               2501_91199785
